---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Customer Success & Customer Operations" current="/customer-success/" description="Richard Allen's experience in customer success, customer experience, SaaS support, technical support, training, team leadership, customer journeys, and customer operations.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Customer Success & Customer Operations</div><h1>Customer relationships backed by strong operating discipline.</h1><p class="lede">My customer-facing work combines relationship management, SaaS and technical support, training, escalation leadership, customer feedback, reporting, and the operating discipline needed to make service clearer and more consistent.</p></div></section>

<section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="stats-grid compact-stats">
    <article class="stat-card teal"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">6 yrs</span></div><div class="metric-label">in HawkSoft customer and technical support</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card blue"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">10+</span></div><div class="metric-label">support professionals led and coached in day-to-day operations</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card gold"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">1+ yr</span></div><div class="metric-label">cross-functional Customer Journey work mapping customer touchpoints</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card violet"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">2</span></div><div class="metric-label">customer-facing technology organizations with SaaS/support experience</div></article>
  </div>

  <div class="experience-path" aria-label="Customer experience lifecycle">
    <div class="path-step"><span>01</span><strong>Understand</strong><small>Listen to customers and identify friction</small></div>
    <div class="path-line"></div>
    <div class="path-step"><span>02</span><strong>Support</strong><small>Troubleshoot, escalate, and keep work moving</small></div>
    <div class="path-line"></div>
    <div class="path-step"><span>03</span><strong>Enable</strong><small>Train customers and staff on better workflows</small></div>
    <div class="path-line"></div>
    <div class="path-step"><span>04</span><strong>Improve</strong><small>Feed patterns back into process and product work</small></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Customer-facing proof</div><h2>Where service, systems, and operations meet.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Selected examples from HawkSoft, The Kotter Group, and related customer-operations work.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">TEAM</div><h3>Support leadership & coaching</h3><p>Provided day-to-day leadership and coaching for a 10+ person customer and technical-support team at HawkSoft, including workflow coverage, escalations, quality review, stand-ups, one-on-one coaching, hiring-team participation, and performance-evaluation support.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">SaaS</div><h3>Technical support & adoption</h3><p>Supported insurance-agency customers using HawkSoft CMS, trained customers and staff on software features and workflows, handled complex escalations, and coordinated database moves between local environments and HawkSoft Online.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">CX</div><h3>Customer Journey work</h3><p>Contributed to a cross-functional Customer Journey / Customer Lifeline initiative lasting more than a year, mapping touchpoints across the customer relationship so teams could see the experience beyond their own department.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">BUILD</div><h3>Building a Customer Experience function</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, established and managed a Customer Experience function, maintained client relationships, gathered customer feedback, and supported service improvement and retention work.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">LEARN</div><h3>Training & customer education</h3><p>Created training documentation, presentations, webinars, online content, and customer communications at The Kotter Group, while HawkSoft work included customer and staff training on troubleshooting, workflows, product changes, and best practices.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">DATA</div><h3>Service reporting & pattern recognition</h3><p>Created operational and management reporting from support and call data, including cleaning and analyzing large Excel exports and turning activity into useful leadership reporting.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="callout"><strong>Best-fit customer-facing roles:</strong> customer operations, customer success leadership, enablement, onboarding, implementation support, service operations, training, and customer-experience work where the focus is improving the system—not personally carrying a high-volume phone queue.</div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
